     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose looks unsafe and I want to check it with you first.\n\n**The problem:** 1,700 mg three times a day adds up to **5,100 mg per day**. The labeled maximum for metformin is:\n- **Immediate-release:** 2,550 mg/day (usually given as 850 mg three times daily)\n- **Extended-release:** 2,000 mg/day\n\nSo this order is about twice the immediate-release maximum. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n2. **Metformin 1,700 mg by mouth per day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n3. Something else, such as an extended-release product or a planned titration from a lower starting dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was confirmed above the labeled maximum. Just let me know which order you want."
      }
     ],
